hi i'm eddie wu and i'm the author of  woo's wonderful world of maths this is a  book about a case of mistaken identity  as a child i thought of mathematics as a  dry and unemotional subject that was all  about memorizing formulas and crunching  meaningless numbers but as i became a  mathematics teacher and sought to  connect this mysterious subject to the  lives of young people i discovered that  it's a practical subject related to  virtually every aspect of daily life i  discovered that it's a surprising  subject that links ideas and concepts  which seem on the surface to have  nothing to do with each other  and i discovered that it's a beautiful  subject that enables us to touch  ultimate reality and come to a newfound  appreciation of the profound patterns  that fill our universe and that's what  this book is all about from the  mind-blowing geometry of sunflowers to  the humble prime numbers upon which the  entire modern economy are built wu's  wonderful world of maths is a guided  tour of my journey through that universe  which shows you some of the discoveries  that opened my eyes to the wonder of  mathematics  i'd summarize wu's wonderful world of  maths as a book about maths for those  who would say they don't like maths i've  written it in the hope that it will  provide you with a light bulb moment  that helps you see what the symbols and  shapes of mathematics are really about  and how they can change your perspective  on everything from life and history to  science and culture i really hope you  like it and that it inspires you to  explore this wonderful world for  yourself
 

